.DS_Store
jj/conf.d/*work*.toml

# Machine-local state that lives beside tracked config
atuin/atuin-receipt.json

# Fish rewrites this on every session and it holds absolute, per-machine paths
fish/fish_variables

# LazyVim rewrites this to record the NEWS.md revision you have dismissed, so it
# diverges per machine. Kept out of the tree entirely rather than just untracked:
# stow reads the filesystem, not the index, so a leftover file here would collide
# with the live one and abort the whole run.
nvim/lazyvim.json

# Regenerated by ~/.config/omarchy/hooks/theme-set.d/zellij-theme-from-omarchy
# on every `omarchy theme set`, so its contents are per-machine output.
zellij/themes/omarchy.kdl

# Everything under these directories is generated or machine-local: fisher
# installs plugin files into $__fish_config_dir, which stow points at this repo,
# and work-machine snippets live in conf.d too. Track only the files we author —
# an allowlist cannot go stale the way a list of plugin filenames would.
# fish_plugins is the source of truth for what fisher reinstalls on each machine.
fish/completions/*
fish/functions/*
fish/themes/*
fish/conf.d/*
!fish/conf.d/abbr.fish

# Per-machine ghostty overrides (see the config-file include at the end of ghostty/config).
ghostty/config.local

# Omarchy writes <file>.bak.<epoch> next to a config each time it rewrites one
# (`omarchy refresh`, the edit-and-reload loop). ~/.config/hypr is stowed as
# per-file symlinks, so today they land there and never in this tree -- this
# guards the case where a directory gets folded and they do.
*.bak.*
